---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import ProjectDetail from '../../components/ProjectDetail.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';

const nav = {
  about: 'About',
  projects: 'Projects',
  experience: 'Experience',
  skills: 'Skills',
  contact: 'Contact',
  menu: 'Open navigation',
  navigation: 'Main navigation',
};

const facts = [
  { label: 'Effort', value: '≈ 200 hours' },
  { label: 'CAD', value: 'Onshape' },
  { label: 'Build', value: 'PA-CF · Bambu Lab X1C' },
  { label: 'Current state', value: 'Revision 1 flight-capable · Revision 2 in CAD' },
];

const sections = [
  {
    title: 'Objective and scope',
    paragraphs: [
      'The development target was a compact, performance-oriented drone with a long-term speed target of 300 km/h, built without an off-the-shelf frame. The target describes the design direction; it has not yet been validated by a speed measurement.',
      'I completed the project independently: component selection, mechanical design, additive manufacturing, soldering, assembly, Betaflight configuration, PID work and flight testing.',
    ],
  },
  {
    title: 'Mechanical and electrical design',
    paragraphs: [
      'The load-bearing frame, body and component packaging were developed through four to five major Onshape iterations. The geometry had to balance stiffness, aerodynamics, cooling, available space, repairability, printability and cost.',
    ],
    table: {
      headers: ['Subsystem', 'Revision 1 choice', 'Design rationale'],
      rows: [
        ['Motors', 'T-Motor Velox V2207 V3 · 2050 KV · 6S', 'Performance at a controlled component cost'],
        ['Flight control', 'SpeedyBee F405 V5 · 55 A stack', 'Reliability prioritized for a central system component'],
        ['Control link', 'RadioMaster RP3 V2 · ELRS', 'Robust link with a compact receiver'],
        ['Navigation', 'HGLRC M100 Pro GPS', 'Required positioning without paying for unused features'],
        ['Propulsion', 'T-Motor T5143S · 5.1-inch · three-blade', 'Matched to the selected 6S powertrain'],
      ],
    },
  },
  {
    title: 'Flight testing and learning',
    paragraphs: [
      'Revision 1 completed one hover test and two controlled flights. Early in testing, the prototype crashed while PID tuning and my own flight experience were still insufficient. I responded by practicing in a simulator and building a second, easier-to-fly training drone before continuing.',
      'The first revision is flight-capable, but top speed, flight time and final mass have not yet been measured under defined conditions.',
    ],
  },
  {
    title: 'Evidence from revision 1',
    paragraphs: [
      'Practical tests revealed three linked weaknesses. Frame resonance complicated PID tuning, while the PA-CF structure became more flexible after absorbing moisture over time. Infrared measurements also showed heat build-up around the flight controller and 4-in-1 ESC. Finally, the top-mounted battery placed too much mass high in the structure.',
    ],
    bullets: [
      'Vibration: revised geometry and a switch from PA-CF to ABS-CF',
      'Cooling: ventilation slots and a new layout for flight controller and ESC',
      'Weight distribution: battery positioned lower, lighter components higher',
      'Control: DJI O4 FPV planned for revision 2 before performance testing',
    ],
  },
  {
    title: 'Revision 2 development process',
    paragraphs: [
      'Revision 2 is currently in its first CAD iteration. The next step is a low-cost PLA print used to identify packaging, assembly and structural weaknesses. The geometry will then be revised and printed again in PLA before the final ABS-CF build. All electronics from revision 1 are planned for reuse.',
      'ABS-CF was selected because the outdoor durability advantage of the more expensive ASA-CF is not required for this use case, while avoiding PA-CF’s moisture sensitivity is central to maintaining predictable stiffness. The trade-off is that stiffness, strength and heat resistance can be lower than with dry PA-CF depending on the exact grade, so the selected material and revised geometry must be validated before high-load testing.',
    ],
  },
  {
    title: 'Commercial engineering',
    paragraphs: [
      'The project was planned against a €700 budget. Documented direct expenditure is approximately €424, including the transmitter, around 1.4 kg of development material and €105 of DJI O4 hardware reserved for revision 2. Excluding that future FPV hardware, documented expenditure is approximately €319. Printer depreciation and unrecorded small consumables are not included.',
    ],
    table: {
      headers: ['Decision', 'Economic reasoning', 'Technical consequence'],
      rows: [
        ['Motors, GPS and material', 'Selected for sufficient performance without paying for unused capability', 'Meet current prototype requirements; limits at the speed target remain to be validated'],
        ['Flight controller and ESC', 'Higher spend on the central, reliability-critical electronics', '55 A stack selected instead of an unbranded alternative'],
        ['Custom printed frame', 'No available frame matched the intended geometry', 'Fast design changes and learning, but 10–15 development prints'],
        ['PLA before ABS-CF', 'Low-cost validation before final material', 'Assembly and structural weaknesses can be corrected before the expensive print'],
        ['Reuse of electronics', 'Preserves most of the project investment', 'Revision 2 focuses spending on mechanics and FPV rather than replacing the system'],
      ],
    },
  },
  {
    title: 'Current result and boundary',
    paragraphs: [
      'Revision 1 proves that the self-designed system can fly and provides concrete design evidence for the next build. It does not yet prove safe operation at the intended high-speed target. A measured speed, flight time and verified take-off mass will be published only after revision 2 has passed controlled mechanical, thermal and flight testing.',
    ],
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  lang="en"
  title="Performance-Oriented Drone Prototype | Raphael Erwig"
  description="Case study: custom CAD, additive manufacturing, flight testing and cost-aware revision of a self-developed drone prototype."
  canonicalPath="/projects/high-speed-drone/"
  enPath="/projects/high-speed-drone/"
  dePath="/de/projekte/high-speed-drohne/"
>
  <Header
    lang="en"
    labels={nav}
    languageHrefs={{ en: '/projects/high-speed-drone/', de: '/de/projekte/high-speed-drohne/' }}
  />
  <ProjectDetail
    backHref="/#projects"
    backLabel="Back to projects"
    eyebrow="Hardware · CAD · Additive Manufacturing"
    title="Iterative development of a performance-oriented drone prototype"
    lead="A self-designed 6S drone that turns practical flight tests, material behavior, thermal measurements and cost trade-offs into a structured second revision."
    status="Revision 1 flight-capable · speed target not yet validated"
    {facts}
    {sections}
    nextLabel="Next case study"
    nextHref="/projects/knife-detection/"
    nextTitle="Live Knife Detection Prototype"
  />
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
